From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:35:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(movement): retain completed client prediction frames

Native 1.26.51.1 protocol 2193 packets distinguish completed fluid motion
from air gravity. At eye Y 103.4815826 a native idle-water frame reports
-0.022315647 blocks per tick, while the previous air approximation reports
-0.0996117 for the matching translated position. Preserve a negotiated
client motion sample instead of reconstructing it from rounded positions.

Consume each sample once at CLIENT_TICK_END, verify that its feet position
matches the standard Java movement stream, and reject non-finite values,
unknown fields and incompatible protocol revisions. Server state and
vehicle prediction remain authoritative; ordinary Java clients retain
their existing approximation. Preserve the sampled floor motion: native
air-floor gameplay reports -0.0784, while water-floor motion is -0.005.

Track local swimming transitions from the same completed frame, including
ViaProxy clients. The client integration sends these frames after normal
Java movement and before the tick-end packet. Keep correction handling,
auth-input construction, frame validation and event state in core.
